Waiting for?

1371
01:04:30,400 --> 01:04:31,780
(The real signal is here)

1372
01:04:32,700 --> 01:04:34,100
(Kill No. 3)

1373
01:04:34,180 --> 01:04:35,340
(Go on. Do it.)

1374
01:04:35,340 --> 01:04:37,620
(Why's he tapping me again?)

1375
01:04:38,000 --> 01:04:39,160
Come on, guys.

1376
01:04:40,280 --> 01:04:41,800
Give your orders already.

1377
01:04:42,680 --> 01:04:44,560
What are you waiting for?

1378
01:04:55,440 --> 01:04:56,280
Mr. Huang, you're out!

1379
01:04:57,240 --> 01:04:58,600
Missed shot. One bullet wasted.

1380
01:05:01,060 --> 01:05:02,420
(Chengcheng still hasn't fired!)

1381
01:05:02,460 --> 01:05:03,580
(The one who fired was...)

1382
01:05:03,580 --> 01:05:04,500
(Him)

1383
01:05:10,080 --> 01:05:10,840
Let me see.

1384
01:05:17,500 --> 01:05:20,140
(Wait, so it was you)

1385
01:05:20,160 --> 01:05:21,400
If you're gonna shoot the wrong person,

1386
01:05:21,400 --> 01:05:22,320
why did it have to be me?

1387
01:05:22,320 --> 01:05:23,760
I was just following orders.

1388
01:05:23,940 --> 01:05:25,260
(Is this what fate feels like?)

1389
01:05:25,360 --> 01:05:26,880
Shouldn't you find yourself
a new boss now?

1390
01:05:28,840 --> 01:05:29,720
You really have no clue, huh?

1391
01:05:32,500 --> 01:05:34,060
(Enjoying the inside scoop)

1392
01:05:36,920 --> 01:05:37,800
This is getting good.

1393
01:05:37,820 --> 01:05:39,840
(Can't stop laughing at his own actions)

1394
01:05:39,840 --> 01:05:40,960
What am I supposed to do now?

1395
01:05:42,520 --> 01:05:43,640
The killer's totally lost.

1396
01:05:43,640 --> 01:05:45,200
Just start shooting randomly.

1397
01:05:45,200 --> 01:05:47,840
You'll look pretty chill doing it.

1398
01:05:51,720 --> 01:05:52,920
(Kill No. 3)
Think carefully.

1399
01:05:52,920 --> 01:05:53,920
(Real signal delivered)
What am I supposed to think about?

1400
01:05:53,920 --> 01:05:55,360
Figure out who your teammate is first.

1401
01:05:55,360 --> 01:05:56,200
I just...

1402
01:05:56,200 --> 01:05:57,000
I know who it is.

1403
01:05:57,000 --> 01:05:57,400
You...

1404
01:05:57,940 --> 01:05:59,040
(Not so sure about that)

1405
01:05:59,040 --> 01:06:00,040
Have you considered

1406
01:06:00,040 --> 01:06:01,480
that you've got the wrong person?

1407
01:06:01,980 --> 01:06:04,140
(Teng, Chengcheng)

1408
01:06:04,160 --> 01:06:05,720
How about this?
You each pick someone for me.

1409
01:06:05,980 --> 01:06:07,540
(Picking a random innocent as his boss)

1410
01:06:09,000 --> 01:06:09,800
That's hilarious.

1411
01:06:09,860 --> 01:06:11,920
(Helpless)

1412
01:06:11,920 --> 01:06:14,800
Jia Yi Bing Ding.

1413
01:06:15,160 --> 01:06:16,560
Jia Yi.

1414
01:06:16,560 --> 01:06:17,560
Jia.

1415
01:06:17,940 --> 01:06:20,220
(Former Boss' order:
Target Jia Bing)

1416
01:06:29,080 --> 01:06:29,960
At this point, I just

1417
01:06:29,960 --> 01:06:32,040
want you to make up your mind.

1418
01:06:33,080 --> 01:06:34,280
Stop putting me through this.

1419
01:06:39,020 --> 01:06:40,140
(Churan)

1420
01:06:40,540 --> 01:06:41,580
(Wang Churan)

1421
01:06:41,620 --> 01:06:44,100
(Grim Reaper's orders: Target Churan,
spotted)

1422
01:06:44,440 --> 01:06:45,320
Teng.

1423
01:06:46,660 --> 01:06:49,620
(Teng or Chengcheng?)

1424
01:06:50,240 --> 01:06:51,080
Think carefully.

1425
01:06:51,080 --> 01:06:52,760
(Take out No. 3)

1426
01:06:52,760 --> 01:06:55,080
Think about how I usually play.

1427
01:06:55,080 --> 01:06:57,200
(Think like Teng)
Think about how I usually play.

1428
01:06:57,760 --> 01:06:59,720
I'm putting everything on this shot.

1429
01:07:01,480 --> 01:07:02,680
If I get this one right,

1430
01:07:02,680 --> 01:07:04,000
I'll know who my boss is.

1431
01:07:04,560 --> 01:07:04,880
Exactly.

1432
01:07:20,520 --> 01:07:21,360
Wang Churan, you're out.

1433
01:07:23,280 --> 01:07:24,640
Game over.

1434
01:07:26,560 --> 01:07:27,680
Was she his boss?

1435
01:07:28,120 --> 01:07:28,720
Nope.

1436
01:07:29,360 --> 01:07:30,720
Who did you think your teammate was?

1437
01:07:31,200 --> 01:07:32,360
I thought it was Chengcheng.

1438
01:07:35,000 --> 01:07:36,200
You didn't suspect me?

1439
01:07:36,200 --> 01:07:37,760
I did after the second shot.

1440
01:07:37,760 --> 01:07:39,200
You didn't think it was me?

1441
01:07:39,780 --> 01:07:41,540
(An answer nobody expected)

1442
01:07:45,000 --> 01:07:45,720
Explain something to me.

1443
01:07:45,720 --> 01:07:47,840
How was he signaling you?

1444
01:07:49,680 --> 01:07:51,320
First, he was the first one

1445
01:07:51,320 --> 01:07:52,520
to get up really awkwardly.

1446
01:07:52,520 --> 01:07:53,600
Then I brought up

1447
01:07:53,600 --> 01:07:54,160
the beautiful scenery,

1448
01:07:54,160 --> 01:07:55,720
and he was the first to put
his arm around me.

1449
01:07:55,720 --> 01:07:57,580
(That's true)

1450
01:07:58,240 --> 01:07:59,280
Can't argue with that.

1451
01:07:59,800 --> 01:08:00,480
Right?

1452
01:08:00,480 --> 01:08:00,880
Yeah.

1453
01:08:01,480 --> 01:08:03,360
And when we took Hu out
in the first round,

1454
01:08:03,360 --> 01:08:04,120
it worked.

1455
01:08:04,460 --> 01:08:06,060
(Another fair point)

1456
01:08:07,620 --> 01:08:08,500
(Frozen in shock)

1457
01:08:08,520 --> 01:08:09,400
Was it you?

1458
01:08:10,440 --> 01:08:11,840
Are you my boss?

1459
01:08:13,240 --> 01:08:14,240
Look me in the eye.

1460
01:08:15,040 --> 01:08:17,000
I can't really judge him
this round either.

1461
01:08:17,480 --> 01:08:20,200
I spent ages exchanging signals
with Chengcheng.

1462
01:08:24,600 --> 01:08:26,640
Didn't you notice me patting
your butt the whole time?

1463
01:08:27,000 --> 01:08:27,440
But,

1464
01:08:27,520 --> 01:08:29,320
in the second round,
I followed him around

1465
01:08:29,320 --> 01:08:31,360
and kept patting his butt.

1466
01:08:31,360 --> 01:08:32,720
You patted mine, so I patted yours.

1467
01:08:34,180 --> 01:08:35,020
(Defeated by life)

1468
01:08:35,060 --> 01:08:37,640
(You're welcome)

1469
01:08:37,640 --> 01:08:39,400
So you listened to me in the first round

1470
01:08:39,400 --> 01:08:40,400
and took him out?

1471
01:08:40,400 --> 01:08:41,960
I followed Chengcheng
in the first round.

1472
01:08:41,980 --> 01:08:43,620
(Sorry, it was me again)

1473
01:08:43,720 --> 01:08:45,720
That was such bad timing.

1474
01:08:45,720 --> 01:08:47,200
Our secret signal

1475
01:08:47,200 --> 01:08:48,680
to identify each other

1476
01:08:48,680 --> 01:08:50,160
was to get up awkwardly.

1477
01:08:50,160 --> 01:08:51,440
He got up first,

1478
01:08:51,440 --> 01:08:52,520
so I got up as well.

1479
01:08:53,000 --> 01:08:55,240
Then I kept patting his butt twice.

1480
01:08:55,240 --> 01:08:56,440
After he called out Hu,

1481
01:08:56,440 --> 01:08:57,680
I was sure we'd got the right guy.

1482
01:08:57,680 --> 01:08:58,160
I thought I'd got it right.

1483
01:08:58,760 --> 01:09:00,560
Turns out he wasn't the one who did it.

1484
01:09:00,560 --> 01:09:01,680
It was him.

1485
01:09:03,600 --> 01:09:04,160
Wait.

1486
01:09:04,160 --> 01:09:04,560
If you were the one

1487
01:09:04,560 --> 01:09:05,440
giving the killer orders,

1488
01:09:05,440 --> 01:09:07,680
you should've been
the first to stand up.

1489
01:09:08,280 --> 01:09:10,320
You have no idea how fast he got up.

1490
01:09:10,680 --> 01:09:11,400
That's true!

1491
01:09:11,400 --> 01:09:12,760
You really don't know how fast he was.

1492
01:09:15,040 --> 01:09:15,680
Three, two, one.

1493
01:09:15,680 --> 01:09:16,320
As soon as the countdown ended...

1494
01:09:16,680 --> 01:09:17,440
What could I do?

1495
01:09:18,200 --> 01:09:19,440
I was the second one up.

1496
01:09:19,440 --> 01:09:21,480
Then everyone else got up like dominoes.

1497
01:09:22,720 --> 01:09:23,920
Neither of us can talk.

1498
01:09:24,440 --> 01:09:26,360
But once I figured out it was you,

1499
01:09:26,360 --> 01:09:28,680
I told you to think carefully.

1500
01:09:28,680 --> 01:09:29,960
I'll give you a punch.

1501
01:09:29,960 --> 01:09:30,760
(A modern-day Master Bodhi?)
No. 3.

1502
01:09:30,760 --> 01:09:32,040
I hit you again, like this.

1503
01:09:33,040 --> 01:09:34,760
But even if I really were the killer,

1504
01:09:34,760 --> 01:09:36,040
you could pat my butt three times

1505
01:09:36,040 --> 01:09:37,200
and I still wouldn't

1506
01:09:37,200 --> 01:09:38,720
know you meant target No. 3.

1507
01:09:40,420 --> 01:09:41,740
(Was I the problem all along?)

1508
01:09:41,800 --> 01:09:44,120
How was I supposed to know
you meant No. 3?

1509
01:09:44,600 --> 01:09:46,080
"Butt" Morse Code.

1510
01:09:46,360 --> 01:09:47,520
What if it's No. 8?

1511
01:09:48,400 --> 01:09:50,080
I'd never pick No. 8.

1512
01:09:52,840 --> 01:09:53,440
That's how you're signaling.

1513
01:09:53,440 --> 01:09:54,280
I'm telling you,

1514
01:09:54,280 --> 01:09:55,680
no one would figure it out

1515
01:09:55,680 --> 01:09:57,480
in a million years.

1516
01:09:58,120 --> 01:09:59,600
Two butt pats mean No. 2?

1517
01:10:00,640 --> 01:10:01,640
Three pats mean No. 3.

1518
01:10:01,640 --> 01:10:03,200
But he never patted my butt.

1519
01:10:03,200 --> 01:10:05,560
Right. I thought it was you.

1520
01:10:06,500 --> 01:10:08,300
(What a spectacular mess)

1521
01:10:08,400 --> 01:10:10,200
Why did you think it was her?

1522
01:10:10,600 --> 01:10:11,920
Teng gave me the idea.

1523
01:10:13,720 --> 01:10:14,600
At first, I thought

1524
01:10:14,600 --> 01:10:15,840
there's no way Teng

1525
01:10:15,840 --> 01:10:16,560
could be my real boss,

1526
01:10:16,560 --> 01:10:17,880
because he never once

1527
01:10:17,880 --> 01:10:18,680
got out of his seat.

1528
01:10:18,680 --> 01:10:19,680
Then Teng suddenly told me,

1529
01:10:19,680 --> 01:10:21,120
Remember how I usually play?

1530
01:10:21,120 --> 01:10:22,280
And it all clicked.

1531
01:10:22,880 --> 01:10:23,600
What clicked?

1532
01:10:23,880 --> 01:10:24,440
I started thinking

1533
01:10:24,440 --> 01:10:25,960
maybe Teng really was my boss.

1534
01:10:25,960 --> 01:10:26,800
So I shot

1535
01:10:26,800 --> 01:10:27,640
Churan.

1536
01:10:27,640 --> 01:10:28,800
You got even more confused.

1537
01:10:28,800 --> 01:10:29,360
What's clicked?

1538
01:10:29,500 --> 01:10:30,460
(Thought he'd cracked it,
but got it all wrong)

1539
01:10:32,440 --> 01:10:34,720
Even at the end,
I was still torn between those two.

1540
01:10:35,200 --> 01:10:36,440
What's this game called again?

1541
01:10:36,740 --> 01:10:39,380
Clueless Killer.

1542
01:10:42,480 --> 01:10:43,520
That just makes

1543
01:10:43,520 --> 01:10:45,320
the two of us clinging to him

1544
01:10:45,320 --> 01:10:45,960
look even dumber.

1545
01:10:46,060 --> 01:10:47,520
(Dumb and Dumber's Guide to Werewolf)

1546
01:10:47,520 --> 01:10:48,160
Look at all this nature.

1547
01:10:49,360 --> 01:10:50,000
Let me see.

1548
01:10:53,760 --> 01:10:55,520
We kept trying to signal him.

1549
01:10:55,540 --> 01:10:57,140
(Should've kept everyone else
out of the way)

1550
01:10:58,400 --> 01:11:00,040
At least we made a comeback this round.

1551
01:11:00,220 --> 01:11:01,800
(Self-congratulations)

1552
01:11:01,800 --> 01:11:02,920
That was a great round.

1553
01:11:03,680 --> 01:11:05,840
Let's congratulate Hu and Bai.

1554
01:11:06,280 --> 01:11:07,240
Oh, I...

1555
01:11:07,240 --> 01:11:08,240
I won a round.

1556
01:11:08,240 --> 01:11:09,200
He won?

1557
01:11:09,880 --> 01:11:11,040
He didn't even realize he'd won.

1558
01:11:13,880 --> 01:11:15,880
We need to tweak the rules.

1559
01:11:16,960 --> 01:11:18,680
Bai, you may have won the game,

1560
01:11:18,680 --> 01:11:19,920
but your performance was...

1561
01:11:19,980 --> 01:11:20,880
(You're one to talk)

1562
01:11:20,880 --> 01:11:23,000
That one point doesn't make up
for how badly you played that round.

1563
01:11:23,840 --> 01:11:24,320
Let's not bring that up.

1564
01:11:24,460 --> 01:11:25,460
(Let's not talk about it)

1565
01:11:25,520 --> 01:11:27,520
We've prepared some local gifts

1566
01:11:27,520 --> 01:11:28,320
for everyone.

1567
01:11:30,720 --> 01:11:31,400
These slate paintings

1568
01:11:31,400 --> 01:11:33,480
are part of Jiuzhaigou's
intangible cultural heritage.

1569
01:11:33,720 --> 01:11:35,920
Each piece is made from local bluestone

1570
01:11:35,920 --> 01:11:38,720
formed over thousands of years.

1571
01:11:39,040 --> 01:11:40,880
The layers symbolize

1572
01:11:40,880 --> 01:11:42,000
a bond that lasts for generations.

1573
01:11:43,960 --> 01:11:45,760
Thank you!

1574
01:12:32,800 --> 01:12:33,680
(Next episode)
Let's try making something new today.

1575
01:12:34,640 --> 01:12:35,640
Smells amazing.

1576
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:36,880
These are the best green beans

1577
01:12:36,880 --> 01:12:37,920
I've ever had.

1578
01:12:38,360 --> 01:12:39,440
This pickled cabbage soup...

1579
01:12:39,440 --> 01:12:40,360
(Don't forget the soup)
Pickled cabbage soup.

1580
01:12:41,660 --> 01:12:42,660
(Top-tier)

1581
01:12:42,760 --> 01:12:44,560
I'll make you some tofu
without stewing it.

1582
01:12:45,200 --> 01:12:46,280
What even is tofu without stewing?

1583
01:12:46,280 --> 01:12:47,400
(Hu gives it a try)
Your tofu's actually pretty good.

1584
01:12:49,800 --> 01:12:51,120
Bro, that first bite blew my mind.

1585
01:12:51,140 --> 01:12:52,540
(Churan's turn to try)

1586
01:12:55,520 --> 01:12:56,320
With food like this,

1587
01:12:56,320 --> 01:12:56,720
who wouldn't

1588
01:12:56,720 --> 01:12:58,000
(What's Chef Huang cooking up?)
feel younger after eating it?

1589
01:12:58,060 --> 01:12:59,140
(Are you convinced yet?)

1590
01:12:59,360 --> 01:13:02,240
(Pick the best match)
Who got confessed to most in school?

1591
01:13:02,400 --> 01:13:04,440
Who'd make the best
children's clothing model?

1592
01:13:04,640 --> 01:13:06,240
What does "best before" mean?

1593
01:13:06,360 --> 01:13:07,480
Someone voted for themselves.

1594
01:13:07,480 --> 01:13:08,560
I'll tell you who.

1595
01:13:09,080 --> 01:13:11,320
(About to get exposed)
You said this vote was anonymous.

1596
01:13:11,320 --> 01:13:13,240
I think I voted for Teng, Bing...

1597
01:13:13,640 --> 01:13:14,480
and myself.

1598
01:13:14,480 --> 01:13:15,660
(No rule against voting for yourself)

1599
01:13:16,370 --> 01:13:19,250
Q: If you were in a novel set
in an imperial harem,

1600
01:13:19,250 --> 01:13:20,920
who would be the emperor's favorite?

1601
01:13:20,920 --> 01:13:21,960
Did you pick Mr. Huang?

1602
01:13:21,960 --> 01:13:23,480
He'd go beat up the emperor.

1603
01:13:24,240 --> 01:13:25,400
They're all tough guys.

1604
01:13:25,400 --> 01:13:27,560
Reverse Story challenge.

1605
01:13:27,560 --> 01:13:28,600
Start wiggling both hands.

1606
01:13:29,880 --> 01:13:31,360
Bro, what's "wiggling" supposed to mean?

1607
01:13:31,480 --> 01:13:33,680
I don't get that Beijing slang.

1608
01:13:33,840 --> 01:13:36,360
Bro, what does "wiggling" mean?

1609
01:13:37,760 --> 01:13:38,480
(Clueless but playing along)
Start wiggling.

1610
01:13:38,480 --> 01:13:39,200
Wiggle your hands.

1611
01:13:39,200 --> 01:13:40,200
What does that even mean?

1612
01:13:41,480 --> 01:13:43,120
You can't even understand Beijing slang.

1613
01:13:43,160 --> 01:13:44,200
That's what he said.

1614
01:13:46,040 --> 01:13:46,640
First three characters.

1615
01:13:46,640 --> 01:13:47,360
Turn up the corners of your mouth.

1616
01:13:48,240 --> 01:13:49,200
Lower your eyelashes.

1617
01:13:52,640 --> 01:13:53,520
One look and she's already lost.

1618
01:13:53,760 --> 01:13:54,400
I kinda forgot.

1619
01:13:54,400 --> 01:13:55,120
Wait, hold on.

1620
01:13:55,120 --> 01:13:56,120
No, what...

1621
01:13:56,120 --> 01:13:56,920
What do I do next?

1622
01:13:56,940 --> 01:13:57,540
(Brain freeze strikes again)

1623
01:13:57,800 --> 01:13:59,040
Our descriptions are fine.

1624
01:13:59,040 --> 01:14:00,120
Our team's problem

1625
01:14:00,120 --> 01:14:00,800
is our memory.

1626
01:14:00,800 --> 01:14:02,340
(Which team will get it right?)

1627
01:14:02,340 --> 01:14:03,520
Sneak a peek and guess.

1628
01:14:03,520 --> 01:14:04,200
(He's got this)
I'll take them down.

1629
01:14:04,200 --> 01:14:04,800
(Bonus episode preview)
Just grab it.

1630
01:14:04,800 --> 01:14:05,520
No need to rip it.

1631
01:14:05,520 --> 01:14:06,500
(Pure muscle)

1632
01:14:06,800 --> 01:14:08,360
(Strength in numbers)
All six of us, hold him down.

1633
01:14:08,440 --> 01:14:09,800
You're telling me six of us
can't beat one guy?

1634
01:14:12,580 --> 01:14:13,060
(Sneak attack)

1635
01:14:16,760 --> 01:14:17,800
Where's Jingyu?

1636
01:14:17,800 --> 01:14:18,280
Jingyu.

1637
01:14:19,280 --> 01:14:20,880
Huang Jingyu!

1638
01:14:25,000 --> 01:14:25,720
(Hand it over)
Help me!

1639
01:14:25,720 --> 01:14:26,560
Got him!

1640
01:14:26,560 --> 01:14:27,560
